description=Linda%20Perhacs%27%20cult%20favorite%20Parallelograms%20instantly%20evokes%20the%20spare%20and%20isolated%20feel%20of%20the%20songs%20and%20the%20production%20on%20Joni%20Mitchell%27s%20first%20albums%2C%20particularly%20her%20debut%20%28largely%20solo%20acoustic%29%20--%20not%20to%20mention%20the%20melodies%2C%20guitar%20playing%2C%20and%20singing.%20It%27s%20not%20a%20photocopy%2C%20however%3B%20it%27s%20hard%20to%20imagine%20Mitchell%20singing%20%22I%27m%20spacing%20out%2C%20I%27m%20seeing%20silences%20between%20leaves%2C%22%20as%20Perhacs%20does%20on%20%22Chimacum%20Rain%2C%22%20unless%20Mitchell%20got%20spiked%20with%20acid%20right%20before%20getting%20on-stage.%20In%20addition%2C%20Perhacs%20is%20adept%20at%20dropping%20unusual%20effects%20and%20arrangements%20into%20the%20mix%2C%20that%20on%20occasion%20have%20a%20mildly%20disquieting%20and%20psychedelic%20vibe.%20Back%20to%20%22Chimacum%20Rain%2C%22%20for%20example%3A%20double-tracked%20voices%20get%20into%20a%20slightly%20hypnotic%2C%20disorienting%20swirl%2C%20and%20suddenly%20move%20into%20a%20half-chanted%20section%20with%20doomy%20background%20notes%20from%20hard-to-identify%20instruments.%20%22Parallelograms%22%20is%20a%20round-like%20vocal%20%28again%20with%20multi-track%20voices%29%2C%20consisting%20of%20exactly%20eight%20words%2C%20that%20without%20warning%20goes%20into%20creepy%20washes%20of%20electronically%20distorted%20voices%2C%20flutes%2C%20and%20rattles.%20Not%20all%20of%20the%20record%20is%20unusual%2C%20though%3B%20much%20of%20it%27s%20just%20attractively%20wistful%2C%20moody%20singer/songwriter%20folk%2C%20sometimes%20with%20an%20engaging%20folk-jazz%20backup%2C%20sometimes%20just%20with%20a%20guitar%2C%20sometimes%20enlivened%20by%20creative%20smudges%20of%20organ%20and%20electric%20guitar.%3Cbr%20/%3E%3Cbr%20/%3E%26copy%20Richie%20Unterberger%20/TiVo
